1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:10,208
Fluids cannot hold a shape, so we describe them with pressure: the normal force per unit area, P equals F over A, measured in pascals.

2
00:00:10,208 --> 00:00:19,934
A drawing pin shows why area matters: the same push from your thumb is gentle on the wide head, but enormous at the tiny point.

